	(text_box "K1401 patient relay: PLACEHOLDER for a made-to-order part (D-64; no such relay exists yet) and J1401 pad connector"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 196.52 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "29a8bcee-1e64-585e-821f-5a6f0626a93c")
	)
	(text_box "PLACEHOLDER (revision 0.3, D-64): no catalogue relay meets the requirement; docs/requirements/patient-relay.md is the specification a maker must meet. The symbol, its\nterminal numbers and the G12 figures below are a wiring placeholder only, not a selected part.\nAt rest (coil off): PT_PAD_A -> NC_A -> PT_FE_A and PT_PAD_B -> NC_B -> PT_FE_B: the pads see only the two front ends (15, 16). Energised: pads -> NO -> HV_OUT_A/B (bridge,\n13). The relay is closed and opened with no current (the sequencer on 12 orders it); it must CARRY 65 A peak for <= 15.5 ms, >= 100 A for 20 ms, 465 A for <= 5 us in a fault\n[UNVERIFIED for every candidate: no maker publishes a pulse/carry rating].\nCandidate search (notes §4): G17 (the design's reference) is a 7.5 kV SF6 relay with 1.0 ohm max contact resistance, 10 A carry, 12 ohm/12 W 100 ms coil and is no longer in\nSensata's catalogue. Best real basis: Sensata/Gigavac G12-12Vdc (DPDT vacuum, 8 kV operating / 10 kV test, 20 mOhm, 10 A carry, 15/9 ms, 12 V 60 ohm coil, -55..+125 C). NO\ncatalogue HV relay has an auxiliary contact: the aux contact is a made-to-order requirement (§B7.2), linked to BOTH poles so a single welded pole is seen (fault 29).\nTerminal numbers 1-10 are project numbers (none published). Coil supply below is sized for the worst coil considered (12 ohm, 12 W, G17 class); with a 60 ohm G12-class coil\nit simply runs at 100 % duty (2.4 W).\nJ1401 (made to order): PAD_A/PAD_B energy contacts (HV_PULSE class, PT_PAD_*), three separated LV contacts: ID (1-Wire DS2431-class EEPROM in the pad plug, D-57), ID_RET (=\nGND), PRESENT (looped to ID_RET inside the plug). No test points on PT_* (R9)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 196.52 27.908)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "97a9c92f-2265-5dbc-a5c9-cd9631886446")
	)
	(text_box "Pad ID (1-Wire) and presence lines: series R + TVS at the connector; aux contact -> K_REST_N"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 242.24 25.4 0)
		(size 175.85 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d0949415-1194-56c1-abb3-8c0929e61aba")
	)
	(text_box "PAD_ID_1W: TVS TPD1E10B06 (bidirectional, VRWM 5.5 V, 12 pF, 6 A 8/20 us) at the contact, then 100 ohm series to the net (2.2 k pull-up on 04). 100 ohm x 4\nmA slave sink = 0.4 V: inside a 3.3 V master's VIL. ADI's own series-R recommendation (DS9503 class) could not be read [UNVERIFIED].\nPAD_PRESENT_N: loop to GND in the plug; TVS at the contact, 1 k series (pull-up 100 k on 04: low = 33 mV). Unplugged / open / unsoldered = high = 'not\nfitted' (safe reading).\nK_REST_N: aux contact AUX_NC closes K_AUX to GND only at rest. 1 k series + TVS so a fault inside the HV relay body cannot put more than a clamp-limited\ncurrent onto the LV board. Open contact, unfitted relay or broken wire = high = 'NOT at rest' (main faults, F-6). See notes 'Contract issues' about what an\nopen contact means to the sequencer (R11)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 242.24 31.75 0)
		(size 175.85 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f3ce5dcb-6de5-59bd-b975-1adbb554d312")
	)
	(text_box "Coil supply input disconnect: Q1401 P-FET, slow turn-on, driven by K_SUPPLY_EN (zero standby draw)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 438.41 25.4 0)
		(size 246.25 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
