				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8d83f874-d527-56c2-8bb5-f4b5f1cb8eed")
	)
	(text_box "A boost converter passes VIN to VOUT when disabled (TPS61089 datasheet §8.3.2), so without this switch the reservoir and DRV110 would sit at VBAT_SYS in standby (aluminium-cap leakage up to 0.5 mA rated, DRV110 0.25\nmA) — against the zero-standby budget of design §11. Q1401 DMP3013SFV (-30 V, VGS +/-25 V, 17 mOhm max at -4.5 V).\nRevision 0.3 (H-1, H-2): K_SUPPLY_EN (main controller; raised when charging for the shock starts, >= 200 ms before RELAY_CMD, FW-12) high -> R1403 -> Q1402 (2N7002, 3.3 V gate) pulls K_PG down through R1402 47 k.\nMiller capacitor C1401 680 nF (was 68 nF) sets the drain slew ~0.15 V/ms -> reservoir pre-charge ~1 A instead of ~7 A [CALC]. Q1401 dissipates ~1/2 C V^2 ~ 0.14 J either way, now over ~45 ms instead of ~6 ms (lower\npeak power; SOA still UNVERIFIED).\nK_SUPPLY_EN low (firmware, or the main domain unpowered: R1421 100 k holds it low) -> R1401 100 k pulls the gate to the source; Q1401 off within ~0.1-0.2 s (tau 100 k x 680 nF; harmless: the boost is disabled at once\nthrough R1413). R1421 is the contract default for K_SUPPLY_EN; R1404 stays the default for K_EN (coil driver off).\nSimulated (sim/rev3-wph/relay_supply_wph.cir): reservoir at 11 V 60-168 ms after K_SUPPLY_EN; battery peak during the pre-charge 1.7-3.3 A including ~0.6 A of other loads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 438.41 31.75 0)
		(size 246.25 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3a889531-a0cb-5a60-a5f9-a57d1032139c")
	)
	(text_box "12 V boost U1401 TPS61089 (VIN 2.7-12 V, VOUT 4.5-12.6 V), EN = K_SUPPLY_EN, peak switch limit 2.0 A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 105.378 0)
		(size 260.64 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "909ab22a-dcf7-53f9-bab5-74849f91db6d")
	)
	(text_box "FB: VREF 1.212 V; R1407 887 k / R1408 100 k -> 11.96 V (OVP 12.7-13.6 V). FSW: R1405 301 k FSW-to-SW -> ~500 kHz (datasheet point).\nILIM (revision 0.3, H-2): R1406 515 k -> 1,030,000 / 515 k = 2.0 A PEAK SWITCH current (SLVSD38C Eq. 2), tolerance -0.8 A (§9.2.2.3) / +0.8 A (EC table at 127 k) -> 1.2-2.8 A. 515 k is OUTSIDE the datasheet's graphed range (Figure\n7-3: 100-400 k): Verify. Being a peak limit with ~2.7 A ripple at 6 V in, the average input at the limit is only ~1-1.8 A, less than the 2.0 A the change order assumed; it still fills the reservoir in <= 168 ms and the coil peak\nphase is carried by the reservoir (>= 8.7 V) [SIM rev3-wph].\nLoad: coil peak 0.86 A x 11.6 V ~ 10 W + DRV110/sense ~0.3 W; the reservoir is pre-filled under K_SUPPLY_EN, so there is no surge at K_EN (I-15).\nL1401 2.2 uH (datasheet nominal; Coilcraft XAL7030-222, Isat >= 9 A [BK, verify]). COUT 3 x 22 uF ceramic on K_VBOOST (datasheet 10-1000 uF effective); the 6.6 mF reservoir sits behind D1401 so the boost loop sees it only while\ncharging it [loop behaviour while charging UNVERIFIED: SIM].\nEN: K_SUPPLY_EN through R1413 100 k (R7: reader may be unpowered while its input ramps); internal 800 k pull-down (SLVSD38C REN) -> 2.9 V high, 1.2 V threshold."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 111.728 0)
		(size 260.64 19.272)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8fc1dafc-f2c4-570b-947f-d5152327905a")
	)
	(text_box "Hold-up reservoir K_VCOIL: D1401 + 2 x 3300 uF 16 V (6.6 mF) — relay stays closed >= 30 ms if the boost or VBAT_SYS fails"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 306.36 124.712 0)
		(size 208.28 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
