		(uuid "f83af42e-3a20-56de-93ac-bbec29905d4b")
	)
	(text_box "RSENSE R1419 0.25 ohm. IPEAK = 0.9 V x 66.67 k / RPEAK / RSENSE: R1415 280 k -> 0.857 A (>= G17 pick-up 8 V / 12 ohm = 0.67 A). IHOLD = 0.15 V x 66.67 k / RHOLD / RSENSE: R1416 80.6 k -> 0.496 A (> G17 worst drop-out 5 V /\n12 ohm = 0.42 A; 'hold at ~50 %', design §B7.2). Hold sense voltage 124 mV (> 30 mV minimum). KEEP C1414 0.33 uF -> 33 ms peak (tKEEP = C x 1e5 s/F): covers pull-in while K_VCOIL is still rising from the battery level. OSC\nto GND -> 20 kHz default (datasheet Eq. 4 text).\nVIN: R1414 1 k from K_VCOIL + C1413 4.7 uF (datasheet Table 3: 1 k at 12 V with EN toggled; internal clamp 15 V; VIN >= 6 V). OUT drives Q1403 gate at VIN (<= 13 V): Q1403 DMN3027LFG has VGS +/-25 V (a +/-12 V part would be\noverstressed). R1420 100 k holds the gate low when U1402 is unpowered.\nEN: K_EN via R1417 10 k with R1418 47 k to GND (the DRV110 EN pin floats HIGH internally: this keeps it low when K_EN is low or open). K_EN low -> gate off at once (CI-8). Revision 0.3: K_EN drives ONLY this enable; VIN is\nalready present from the pre-charged reservoir; start-up delay <= 50 us (SLVSBA8G tD).\nFast release: coil current at turn-off goes K_COIL_L -> D1402 SS34 -> D1403 SMBJ10A (VBR 11.1-12.3 V) -> K_VCOIL: ~ -12.8 V across the coil instead of -0.5 V (release time is in the timing budget, R-12). The same path\nfreewheels the 20 kHz hold PWM (fast decay: more ripple and loss in hold, acceptable for <= 90 ms). Drain peak = 13.2 V + 12.3 V + ~1 V + 0.5 V ~ 27 V < 30 V VDS (90 %) [CALC].\nThe 90 ms on-time cap and the <= 60 ms start window are on 12_bridge_logic (contract §8); this sheet only obeys K_EN. STATUS (open drain) is not read: no contract net."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
